    "dateCreated": "2018-12-01",
    "datePublished": "2023-04-18",
    "description": "samurai (Structured Adaptive mesh and MUlti-Resolution based on Algebra of Intervals) is a header-only C++ library for numerical simulation on adaptive Cartesian meshes. Mesh adaptation methods come in several kinds: patch-based AMR, cell-based AMR, and cell-based or point-based multiresolution. Other open source libraries each cover one kind: AMReX for patch-based AMR, p4est and PABLO for cell-based adaptation.\n\nsamurai implements all of these methods on one data structure. The mesh is stored as intervals, and a set algebra on these intervals finds the subsets of cells that a numerical scheme works on.",
    "downloadUrl": "https://github.com/hpc-maths/samurai/releases",
